# Edge-legend parametric family

`adapter.py` is the native entry point. `program({'fill_scope':'all'})` returns the exact bytes of the local `canonical.rkt`, which equals the root reference. The only alternative is `largest_per_owner`, retaining all maximum-area ties independently for each cavity-owner color. No program or output comes from a stored original example.

```python
episode = adapter.generate(seed=17, settings={'fill_scope':'largest_per_owner'}, demos=2, queries=4)
```

Counts are independent:2–6 demos and1–4 queries. The complete banks are generated before taking prefixes; the four-query bank is privately shuffled. Seeds are exact integers0..2**63-1 and boolean counts/settings are rejected. Keep the episode, directory listing, settings, program and future queries private; expose only one content-hashed query view at a time.

`prototype.py` supplies self-contained `scene`, `analyze`, `solve` and strict `validate_grid` functions. Black is the background. A unique dense2×N/N×2 legend sits on one decoding edge; its outer line maps to the inward line. An eight-neighbor black moat separates it from other foreground. Eligible cavities are four-connected zero regions with one cardinal boundary owner and no canvas-edge contact. Mixed/unmapped/open regions remain unchanged.

The alternative's causal chain is cavity geometry → per-owner maximum areas → selected cavities → input-legend colors. A protected30×30 witness substitutes a global maximum and changes13 cells. This is not a constant color-map composition.

Current evidence lives in WORK/checks/public_eval_dbff022c/: `preflight/`, `family-tests-v2/`, `rival-v3/`, `inference/`, `generator/`, `boundary-v2.json`, `causal/`, and `export/`. See root notes for counts, resolved failures and scope. Task tests use their own library-layout root; they do not require a canonical ledger to locate unregistered generator files.

The source inventory and preflight establish reviewer readiness only. Owner registration and unchanged native qualification/acceptance remain separate.
